1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,744
In Eswatini, one king still chooses the
prime minister.

2
00:00:04,244 --> 00:00:08,831
Yet here you can walk among zebras, follow
rhinos on foot, and stand in a

3
00:00:08,851 --> 00:00:10,365
mine older than farming.

4
00:00:10,865 --> 00:00:13,737
In this country, a safari can mean a
bicycle.

5
00:00:14,237 --> 00:00:17,013
Six reasons to go. And number five is
older than farming itself.

6
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:21,359
Eswatini sits between South Africa and
Mozambique, and about one point two

7
00:00:21,379 --> 00:00:22,633
million people liv here.

8
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:25,702
It is a little smaller than New Jersey.

9
00:00:26,202 --> 00:00:29,294
Until twenty eighteen, it was called
Swaziland.

10
00:00:29,314 --> 00:00:30,970
Then the king renamed it.

11
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:37,024
Its king, Mswati III the Third, has
reigned since nineteen eighty-six.

12
00:00:37,524 --> 00:00:39,028
Mbabane is the administrative capital.

13
00:00:39,048 --> 00:00:40,853
Lobamba is the royal and legislative
capital.

14
00:00:41,353 --> 00:00:43,303
One. Walk among the zebras.

15
00:00:43,803 --> 00:00:48,187
Mlilwane Wildlife Sanctuary is the
country's oldest protected area.

16
00:00:48,207 --> 00:00:53,334
It has no big predators, so you can
explore on foot, by bike, or on horseback.

17
00:00:53,834 --> 00:00:58,806
Zebras and antelope graze beside the
trails, and hippos wallow in the dams.

18
00:00:58,826 --> 00:01:01,422
Just keep a wary eye on the crocodiles.

19
00:01:01,922 --> 00:01:03,392
Two. Follow the rhinos.

20
00:01:03,892 --> 00:01:07,915
Hlane Royal National Park, once a royal
hunting ground, is the country's

21
00:01:07,935 --> 00:01:09,206
biggest protected area.

22
00:01:09,226 --> 00:01:12,202
It covers about two hundred twenty square
kilometers.

23
00:01:12,702 --> 00:01:14,156
The name means wilderness.

24
00:01:14,176 --> 00:01:17,917
White rhinos roam free, and guides take
you on walks to find them.

25
00:01:18,417 --> 00:01:22,206
Lions and elephants liv in a separate
area, open only on guided drives.

26
00:01:22,706 --> 00:01:25,150
Three. Climb a mountain made of one rock.

27
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:30,268
Sibebe Rock, near Mbabane, is a granite
dome about three billion years old.

28
00:01:30,768 --> 00:01:34,157
Community guides run the hikes, and the
wet rock glitters after rain.

29
00:01:34,657 --> 00:01:36,701
Four. Watch craftspeople at work.

30
00:01:37,201 --> 00:01:41,028
At Ngwenya Glass, workers blow glass by
mouth from recycled bottles.

31
00:01:41,528 --> 00:01:45,482
Swazi Candles has made candles near
Malkerns since nineteen eighty-two.

32
00:01:45,502 --> 00:01:48,581
Artists there shape hot wax into colorful
works of art.

33
00:01:49,081 --> 00:01:52,431
Next, a cave where people were digging
long before farming began.

34
00:01:52,931 --> 00:01:56,204
Five. Stand in the oldest known ochre mine
in the world.

35
00:01:56,704 --> 00:01:58,131
It is called Lion Cavern.

36
00:01:58,151 --> 00:02:01,738
Ngwenya means crocodile, named for a
mountain shaped like one.

37
00:02:02,238 --> 00:02:05,458
Researchers dated the digging to about
forty-eight thousand years ago.

38
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:11,236
Ochre makes a red pigment, so these first
miners were already reshaping their world.

39
00:02:11,736 --> 00:02:15,621
A ranger walks you up an easy trail and a
steel staircase to the cave.

40
00:02:15,641 --> 00:02:18,207
The view over the old mine is worth the
climb.

41
00:02:18,707 --> 00:02:21,769
The site is on the tentative list for
UNESCO World Heritage status.

42
00:02:22,269 --> 00:02:25,317
Six. Meet the culture, starting with one
word.

43
00:02:25,817 --> 00:02:30,453
Sawubona. It means hello, and it is often
explained as, I see you.

44
00:02:30,953 --> 00:02:31,826
Reply, yebo.

45
00:02:31,846 --> 00:02:38,101
Then try sishwala, a thick maize porridge,
and wash it down with emasi, soured milk.

46
00:02:38,601 --> 00:02:42,179
Come in late August or early September for
the Reed Dance.

47
00:02:42,199 --> 00:02:46,770
For about eight days, tens of thousands of
unmarried young women gather at

48
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:47,907
the royal village.

49
00:02:48,407 --> 00:02:52,378
Come in May for Bushfire, a three-day
music festival in the Malkerns Valley.

50
00:02:52,398 --> 00:02:55,497
In twenty twenty-six, it drew twenty-three
thousand people.

51
00:02:55,997 --> 00:03:00,826
And in December or January comes Incwala,
the sacred ceremony of kingship

52
00:03:00,846 --> 00:03:04,632
and renewal. Many parts forbid
photography, so just watch.

53
00:03:05,132 --> 00:03:08,411
English is an official language, and cars
drive on the left.

54
00:03:08,431 --> 00:03:11,874
The lilangeni is pegged one to one with
the South African rand.

55
00:03:11,894 --> 00:03:14,973
The best time to go is the dry season, May
to September.

56
00:03:15,473 --> 00:03:16,582
That was Eswatini.

57
00:03:16,602 --> 00:03:18,778
Which country should we visit next?

58
00:03:18,798 --> 00:03:20,303
Tell me in the comments.

